==Original Issue==

If you open an article, bookmark it, start playing, then while it's playing, go to bookmarks and open another bookmarked file that was already playing in the past and then tap on it, you get the resume playing from prior location dialog, and then you tap that, then both the prior article that you started playing and the new one that you resumed on start playing simultaneously, just talking over each other. There's two streams of audio happening at the same time. Seems like hopefully a kind of simple fix, that just once you're starting a new stream of audio, or even just clicking on a bookmark so that you've loaded another page should terminate the existing audio stream.
