Changes
-------
1. app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml — added android:launchMode="singleTask" to
   .MainActivity so every intent (bookmark open, notification tap, launcher, deep link)
   converges on the single reading-screen instance and is delivered via onNewIntent().
2. app/src/main/java/cloud/morris/wcast/BookmarksActivity.kt — openInMain() now uses
   FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TOP or FLAG_ACTIVITY_SINGLE_TOP.
3. app/src/main/java/cloud/morris/wcast/tts/WcastMediaService.kt — appContentIntent()
   now uses FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TOP or FLAG_ACTIVITY_SINGLE_TOP so a notification tap
   reuses the screen.
4. app/src/main/java/cloud/morris/wcast/MainViewModel.kt — openBookmarkedArticle()
   now calls stopSpeaking() immediately (before launching the load coroutine) so the
   currently playing stream is terminated the moment a bookmark is selected.

Why this fixes the bug
----------------------
A single MainActivity instance means a single MainViewModel => a single SpeechController
=> a single live MediaPlayer. Reusing the reading screen (instead of stacking a second
one) removes the duplicate controller that produced the two simultaneous streams, and
the earlier stopSpeaking() guarantees the old stream stops before the new article loads.

